{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-9e975e85347e9876", "type": "tool_result", "content": "1700\tsublinear duration weight so that long segments do not dominate. Anchor tokens (the first frame of\n1701\teach segment) are selected by density-aware farthest-point sampling (DA-FPS). Starting from the\n1702\tdensest prototype, we iteratively add the token that maximizes\n1703\t(1−simmaxsel)⋅ρ(1-\\text{sim}_{\\max}^{\\text{sel}})\\cdot\\rho, where simmaxsel\\text{sim}_{\\max}^{\\text{sel}} is the maximum\n1704\tcosine similarity to already-selected tokens and the density ρ\\rho is a token’s mean top-kk cosine\n1705\tsimilarity weighted by how many tokens it covers. DA-FPS thus rewards both density and novelty, keeping a\n1706\tdiverse, high-coverage set of representatives rather than clustering around a few peaks.\n1707\tNon-anchor frames keep only the tokens least similar to their paired anchor (deduplication), dropping\n1708\tcontent the anchor already represents. Audio tokens are not pruned in this stage. The pre-LLM budget\n1709\tcounts audio and video tokens together: if the total budget is BB and all NAN_{A} audio tokens are kept,\n1710\twe allocate the remaining B−NAB-N_{A} tokens to video. The video keep ratio is then chosen to retain exactly\n1711\tthis number of video tokens.\n1712\t\n1713\tAppendix B Additional Efficiency Results\n1714\t\n1715\tThe 33B backbone reproduces the 77B inference-speed ordering: A-PACK has the lowest prefilling time (Figure S1), the shortest time-to-first-token, and the highest decoding throughput (Figure S2). Table S2 further shows the best compressed-model accuracy together with the lowest memory and largest speedups on WorldSense.\n1716\t\n1717\tMethod\n1718\tBenchmark\n1719\t\n1720\tFLOPs↓\\downarrow\n1721\t\n1722\tPre-LLM\n1723\t\n1724\tInner-LLM\n1725\t\n1726\tAVUT (%)\n1727\t\n1728\tDailyOmni (%)\n1729\t\n1730\tFull\n1731\t\n1732\tFull\n1733\t\n1734\t62.5\n1735\t\n1736\t61.6\n1737\t\n1738\t100%\n1739\t\n1740\tRandom\n1741\t\n1742\tRandom\n1743\t\n1744\t57.3\n1745\t\n1746\t55.0\n1747\t\n1748\t35.8%\n1749\t\n1750\tRandom\n1751\t\n1752\tA-PACK\n1753\t\n1754\t57.7\n1755\t\n1756\t53.8\n1757\t\n1758\t28.8%\n1759\t\n1760\tA-PACK\n1761\t\n1762\tRandom\n1763\t\n1764\t59.0\n1765\t\n1766\t56.2\n1767\t\n1768\t35.8%\n1769\t\n1770\tA-PACK\n1771\t\n1772\tFastV\n1773\t\n1774\t50.6\n1775\t\n1776\t55.7\n1777\t\n1778\t30.0%\n1779\t\n1780\tA-PACK\n1781\t\n1782\tDyCoke\n1783\t\n1784\t59.6\n1785\t\n1786\t56.1\n1787\t\n1788\t37.3%\n1789\t\n1790\tA-PACK\n1791\t\n1792\tA-PACK\n1793\t\n1794\t60.6\n1795\t\n1796\t55.4\n1797\t\n1798\t28.8%\n1799\t\n1800\tTable S3: Stage-combination ablation on Qwen2.5-Omni-3B (columns as in Table 3).\n1801\t\n1802\tMethod\n1803\tStage\n1804\tCost\n1805\tBenchmark\n1806\t\n1807\tPre-\n1808\tLLM\n1809\t\n1810\tInner-\n1811\tLLM\n1812\t\n1813\tPrefill\n1814\tFLOPs\n1815\t\n1816\tAVUT\n1817\t\n1818\tWorld\n1819\tSense\n1820\t\n1821\tDaily\n1822\tOmni\n1823\t\n1824\tAvg.\n1825\t\n1826\tQwen2.5-Omni-7B\n1827\t\n1828\tFull\n1829\t–\n1830\t–\n1831\t\n1832\t100%\n1833\t\n1834\t64.5\n1835\t\n1836\t46.8\n1837\t\n1838\t63.0\n1839\t\n1840\t100%\n1841\t\n1842\tPre only\n1843\t✓\n1844\t–\n1845\t\n1846\t44.6%\n1847\t\n1848\t64.5\n1849\t\n1850\t46.2\n1851\t\n1852\t59.4\n1853\t\n1854\t97.7%\n1855\t\n1856\tA-PACK\n1857\t✓\n1858\t✓\n1859\t\n1860\t29.9%\n1861\t\n1862\t64.2\n1863\t\n1864\t45.8\n1865\t\n1866\t60.5\n1867\t\n1868\t97.8%\n1869\t\n1870\tQwen2.5-Omni-3B\n1871\t\n1872\tFull\n1873\t–\n1874\t–\n1875\t\n1876\t100%\n1877\t\n1878\t62.5\n1879\t\n1880\t46.2\n1881\t\n1882\t61.6\n1883\t\n1884\t100%\n1885\t\n1886\tPre only\n1887\t✓\n1888\t–\n1889\t\n1890\t41.8%\n1891\t\n1892\t60.5\n1893\t\n1894\t45.3\n1895\t\n1896\t56.8\n1897\t\n1898\t95.7%\n1899\t\n1900\tA-PACK\n1901\t✓\n1902\t✓\n1903\t\n1904\t23.1%\n1905\t\n1906\t60.6\n1907\t\n1908\t45.3\n1909\t\n1910\t57.8\n1911\t\n1912\t96.3%\n1913\t\n1914\tTable S4: Sequential stage ablation: Pre only keeps the pre-