to-first-token, and the highest decoding throughput (Figure S2). Table S2 further shows the best compressed-model accuracy together with the lowest memory and largest speedups on WorldSense.\n\nMethod\nBenchmark\n\nFLOPs↓\\downarrow\n\nPre-LLM\n\nInner-LLM\n\nAVUT (%)\n\nDailyOmni (%)\n\nFull\n\nFull\n\n62.5\n\n61.6\n\n100%\n\nRandom\n\nRandom\n\n57.3\n\n55.0\n\n35.8%\n\nRandom\n\nA-PACK\n\n57.7\n\n53.8\n\n28.8%\n\nA-PACK\n\nRandom\n\n59.0\n\n56.2\n\n35.8%\n\nA-PACK\n\nFastV\n\n50.6\n\n55.7\n\n30.0%\n\nA-PACK\n\nDyCoke\n\n59.6\n\n56.1\n\n37.3%\n\nA-PACK\n\nA-PACK\n\n60.6\n\n55.4\n\n28.8%\n\nTable S3: Stage-combination ablation on Qwen2.5-Omni-3B (columns as in Table 3).\n\nMethod\nStage\nCost\nBenchmark\n\nPre-\nLLM\n\nInner-\nLLM\n\nPrefill\nFLOPs\n\nAVUT\n\nWorld\nSense\n\nDaily\nOmni\n\nAvg.\n\nQwen2.5-Omni-7B\n\nFull\n–\n–\n\n100%\n\n64.5\n\n46.8\n\n63.0\n\n100%\n\nPre only\n✓\n–\n\n44.6%\n\n64.5\n\n46.2\n\n59.4\n\n97.7%\n\nA-PACK\n✓\n✓\n\n29.9%\n\n64.2\n\n45.8\n\n60.5\n\n97.8%\n\nQwen2.5-Omni-3B\n\nFull\n–\n–\n\n100%\n\n62.5\n\n46.2\n\n61.6\n\n100%\n\nPre only\n✓\n–\n\n41.8%\n\n60.5\n\n45.3\n\n56.8\n\n95.7%\n\nA-PACK\n✓\n✓\n\n23.1%\n\n60.6\n\n45.3\n\n57.8\n\n96.3%\n\nTable S4: Sequential stage ablation: Pre only keeps the pre-LLM stage, and A-PACK adds the\ninner-LLM stage. Prefill FLOPs are relative ratio versus Full tokens. Avg. is the mean of\nAVUT/WorldSense/Daily(Omni) relative to Full.\n\n(a) Gate-threshold sensitivity\n\n(b) Fine-blend sensitivity\n\n(c) Pre-LLM retention ratio (%)\n\nFigure S4: Additional sensitivity analyses. Red circles denote\nthe highest scores.\n\nComponent\n\nAxis (selected)\n\nTested value(s)\n\nΔ\\Delta accuracy (points)\n\nSegmentation\n\nContinuity τsim\\tau_{\\mathrm{sim}} (0.970.97)\n\n0.93, 0.95, 0.990.93,\\ 0.95,\\ 0.99\n\n+1.76,+0.75,−2.51+1.76,\\ +0.75,\\ -2.51\n\nSmoothing σ\\sigma (1.01.0)\n\n0.5, 1.5, 2.00.5,\\ 1.5,\\ 2.0\n\n0.00, 0.00,−1.260.00,\\ 0.00,\\ -1.26\n\nToken selection\n\nDA-FPS power (0.50.5)\n\n0.3, 0.7,